title: 'Gnomon: Orca follow-ups, P8-D98 client-API move, and drain/resume all built and merged to feat/gnomon'
summary: |-
  A single orchestrated session on 2026-10-19 cleared the remaining Gnomon backlog. Every slice was reviewed by Aegis, fixed, and run through all three suites before merging.

  Work merged:
  - Hardening follow-ups (T-011): Linux ready FIFO, pidfile reclaim, re-probe, pre-auth AUTH.
  - Security cleanups (T-016): daemon status pins the kernel key; client-pinning audit.
  - Onboarding follow-ups (T-006): Cmd-Q cleanup, setup routing tests, portal gates, headless Chrome smoke test.
  - gnomon guide (T-015): compiled in, with honesty check G-HON-08.
  - Flakes fixed: T-008 and T-012.
  - The P8-D98 batched client-API move (T-001), in slices:
    - A0: contracts.
    - A1: rules revoke.
    - A2: effect.failed and decisionSig v2.
    - A3: gui.open with a fair launch cap.
    - A4: {logId, seq} cursor.
    - B0: daemon.stop verb plus the Touch ID card.
  - Session sandbox: transcripts can be written under ~/.claude/projects. The projects dir itself can't be deleted, and hardlinks were measured as refused.
  - Drain/resume (T-014):
    - B1: drain on upgrade, recording clean vs interrupted turns.
    - B2: resume before the orphan sweep via --resume. Interrupted sessions come back idle. A permit live at drain carries over. Old cards expire.

  Founder decision dialogs: TD-2026-10-19-946, 908, 252, 648, 528, 947, 814, 339, 476, 739. The P-resume probe was run by the founder and recorded as evidence. The final unreleased clientApiId is sha256:7c006597…5a40. A decision-id collision bug was found and filed as T-020; the overwritten decision was restored.
symbols_touched:
  - $daemon-lifecycle
  - '#socket'
  - '#gnomon-contracts'
