decisions:
  - id: TD-2026-10-19-947
    decision: 'Law 3 gets a human-device tier: 12 kernel verbs + 3 human-device verbs + 2 relays'
    rationale: Keeps abiId and modAbiId stable; human-only verbs never widen agent reach
  - id: TD-2026-10-19-814
    decision: Sessions may write ~/.claude/projects; turns cut at the deadline resume idle
    rationale: The probe showed no transcript means no resume, and that a mid-tool kill re-runs the tool on continue
  - id: TD-2026-10-19-739
    decision: A permit live at drain carries over with a fresh expiry, never minted
    rationale: The 60-minute TTL would otherwise stop most real sessions on every upgrade
errors_encountered:
  - description: A stale GUI bundle after the contracts move failed CI on every platform
    resolution: Re-embedded; the GUI suite now always runs before a push
  - description: paradigm_decision overwrote TD-946 on an id collision
    resolution: Restored by hand, law-3 moved to 947, filed T-2026-10-19-020
  - description: 'Linux CI: libuv''s stdio pipe is a socketpair, which cannot be re-opened via /proc'
    resolution: A private FIFO channel on linux
learnings:
  - 'Run the gnomon-gui suite, including its bundle --check, before every push: gnomon-gui bundles gnomon-contracts'
  - 'Builders hit 50 turns on almost every slice: brief them at ~30 turns of scope or expect a resume'
  - Every security-touching slice got Aegis findings worth fixing; review before merge paid off every time
  - Merging parallel branches needs a hand check of daemon.ts humanVerbs wiring and of duplicate imports
